&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Lead Researcher&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Research &amp;amp; Insights team to design and implement user research programs for a new Mobile/PC game in development in the US on remote basis.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play every day—whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who develop, publish, and innovate in the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people around the world daily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to executing high-impact research, this role serves as a strategic collaboration for the product, driving the research roadmap for the product and influencing key design decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead research initiatives to drive a deeper understanding of the player experience across game development and live operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a driving strategic partner to product leadership, identifying where research can inform design vision, roadmap priorities, and player experience strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and drive the end-to-end user experience research function, from defining research strategy through execution, synthesis, and delivery of insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with game development, strategy, and leadership teams to translate insights into KPIs, product decisions, and solutions to player experience&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, execute, and present high-impact quantitative and qualitative user experience research studies in partnership with consumer insights, research operations, and cross-functional teams (e.g., Game Design, UX Design, Product Management, Production, Marketing, Data Analytics, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate research findings into clear, actionable recommendations that influence design decisions and measurable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As required, manage external research partners, ensuring cost-effective methods with clear objectives and timely, high-quality results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define, evolve, and scale research methodologies, frameworks, and best practices across Scopely’s Research &amp;amp; Insight’s user research division&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and support other user researchers, contributing to the growth and maturity of the team’s capabilities and impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a best-in-class user experience researcher who embodies Scopely’s &lt;em&gt;Care Deeply, Iterate to Greatness, &lt;/em&gt;and&lt;em&gt; Play to Win&lt;/em&gt; tenets—someone who takes ownership, moves with efficiency, and holds themselves to the highest standards. In this role, you will be expected to deliver actionable and transformative insights to your assigned product, while also helping to elevate the craft and maturity of research across the whole of Scopely’s user research division.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate has a passion for games, a strong foundation in mixed-method user experience research (e.g., surveys, usability playtests, IDIs, focus groups), and the ability to partner effectively with cross-functional stakeholders at all levels of the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree required, preferably in Psychology, Human-Computer Interaction, Game Design, Social Science, or a related field; MBA, Master’s, or PhD preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience conducting end-to-end user experience research in gaming at either a developer/publisher or research agency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in mixed-method user experience research, with demonstrated ability to select and apply appropriate methodologies across various stages of production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of driving measurable product or player experience improvements through research insights from a variety of sources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting product strategy and roadmap decisions through research in complex, cross-functional environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with and managing external research vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal, analytical, and project management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to influence senior stakeholders and align cross-functional teams using evidence-based insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scaling or improving research practices and tools within a team or organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for gaming and a strong understanding of core loops and monetization of mobile/PC games&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail, intellectual curiosity, and comfort tackling complex and ambiguous problem spaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quarterly travel for in-person research at our LA-based Lab required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Familiarity with online survey tools (e.g., Qualtrics, SurveyGizmo/Alchemer) and remote testing platforms (e.g., PlaytestCloud, UserTesting)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advanced AI analysis or analytics tools such as SPSS and SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidates with experience in social play or midcore live-service games strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For candidates in CA, CO, NJ, NY, and WA, the annual salary range is provided below. In addition to base pay, employees may be eligible for equity, bonuses, and a comprehensive benefits package, including healthcare benefits, retirement benefits, pet insurance, paid holidays, paid Scopely free days, and unlimited paid time off. Base pay offered may vary depending on job-related knowledge, skills, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;CA, CO, NJ, NY, and WA Annual Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$169,600&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$253,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Scopely&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is a leading video game and global interactive entertainment company, home to many of the world’s most beloved and enduring experiences, including two of the most successful mobile games of all-time “MONOPOLY GO!” and “Pokémon GO,” along with “Stumble Guys,” “Star Trek™ Fleet Command,” “MARVEL Strike Force,” “WWE Champions,” the Scrabble® franchise, “Yahtzee® With Buddies,” and many others. Across mobile, web, PC, and console, Scopely creates, develops, publishes, and live-operates one of the most diversified and award-winning portfolios in the games industry — bringing hundreds of millions of players together through a shared love of play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2011, Scopely is powered by its exceptional team — including thousands of world-class gamemakers around the globe, a distinctive tenet-driven culture, and its proprietary technology platform, Playgami. Together, these strengths have fueled Scopely’s position as the #1 mobile games company in the U.S. and #2 globally, generating more than $10 billion in lifetime revenue. Whether building global sensations like “MONOPOLY GO!” from the ground up, or expanding through strategic acquisitions, including the FoxNext, GSN, and Scopely Explore games businesses — Scopely consistently delivers experiences players love today and return to for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognized multiple times as one of the &quot;100 Most Influential Companies in the World&quot; by TIME magazine and one of Fast Company&#39;s &quot;World&#39;s Most Innovative Companies&quot; and “Best Workplaces for Innovators,” Scopely believes that video games can be a force for good — creating meaningful connections, vibrant communities, and making life better through play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely has global operations and partners across four continents in more than a dozen countries worldwide. For more information, visit: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/&quot;&gt;https://www.scopely.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notice to Candidates: Scopely will never request payment or financial information during the application or hiring process. Please apply only through our official &lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;website&lt;/a&gt; and verify that all Talent Partner communications come from an email address ending in @&lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;scopely.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Should you have any questions or encounter any fraudulent requests/emails/websites, please immediately contact recruiting@scopely.com. Our job applicant privacy policies are available here: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/job-applicant-privacy-notice-for-ca-residents&quot;&gt;California Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/eea-and-uk-job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;EEA/UK Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employment at Scopely is based solely on a person&#39;s merit and qualifications. Scopely does not discriminate against any employee or applicant because of race, creed, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding), or any other basis protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Discord has a highly engaged community of millions of daily active users who use the platform for many different reasons, but there’s one thing that nearly everyone does: &lt;strong&gt;play video games.&lt;/strong&gt; Discord plays a uniquely important role in the future of gaming, and we are focused on making it easier and more fun for people to hang out before, during, and after playing games.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Creators are people who build audiences across the internet: influential voices whose communities listen to them and want to spend time together. Many of those communities already live on Discord, but our relationship with creators has grown organically. We have an opportunity to listen more closely, serve them more intentionally, and build a relationship that reflects the role they play on our platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a Senior Staff Program Manager to build Discord’s approach to creators from the ground up. You’ll begin with a selected group of creators already using Discord, build the fundamentals that serve them well, and develop programs that make their experience on Discord better. Over time, you’ll turn what works into programs that can serve creators at scale and, eventually, give new creators more reasons to choose Discord. This is a senior individual contributor role for someone who can lead through judgment, relationships, and execution. You’ll report to the Director of Marketing, Player Communications and partner closely with Support, Product, Marketing, Communications, Partnerships, Policy, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build Discord’s creator strategy from the bottom up, starting with direct conversations and a clear understanding of what creators already on Discord need from us.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring together the creator work that exists across Discord today, establish clear ownership, and turn a collection of early efforts into a coherent program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define who we mean by creators and develop an initial approach for selecting and serving a trusted group across games, platforms, formats, and communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create more than one program for creators, beginning with the fundamentals: accelerated support, clear paths for escalation, and reliable channels for two-way communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with important creators directly. Understand how they use Discord, help them solve meaningful problems, and build trust by following through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a creator council or network that gives us a consistent view of what creators are seeing, where Discord is falling short, and what would make the platform more useful to them and their communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build systems and playbooks that let a selected program grow over time without losing the relationships and responsiveness that made it valuable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you should have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong passion for Discord and/or gaming, and an appreciation for the creators and communities we serve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in creator partnerships, community, platform programs, marketing, product partnerships, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply familiar with how creators build audiences, operate their businesses, and manage communities across platforms like YouTube, Twitch, TikTok, Instagram, Patreon, Reddit, and Discord.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have built and operated creator or partner programs at scale, and you understand how to begin with a selected group without designing something that can never grow beyond it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Biased to ship and iterate. You can launch a useful first version, learn from it, and raise the ambition over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable leading as an individual contributor. You create alignment and momentum across teams without relying on headcount or reporting lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An excellent cross-functional partner across Support, Product, Marketing, Comms, Partnerships, Policy, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have built a creator, partner, ambassador, advisory, or VIP program for a consumer platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have designed accelerated support or escalation programs for influential users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have worked directly with gaming creators and understand the relationship between creators, games, and communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have built programs involving product access, creator events, recognition, or discovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have helped turn creator feedback into product changes, policies, or platform strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have built a program that began with a small trusted group and expanded without losing what made it valuable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is $256,000 to $288,000 + equity + benefits. Our salary ranges are determined by role and level. Within the range, individual pay is determined by additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Please note that the compensation details listed in US role postings reflect the base salary only, and do not include equity, or benefits.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Candidates must reside in or be willing to relocate to the San Francisco Bay Area (Alameda, Contra Costa, Marin, Napa, San Francisco, San Mateo, Santa Clara, Solano, and Sonoma counties). Relocation assistance may be available.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Discord?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Discord plays a uniquely important role in the future of gaming. We&#39;re a multiplatform, multigenerational and multiplayer platform that helps people deepen their friendships around games and shared interests, and helps developers build and grow their businesses. We believe games give us a way to have fun with our favorite people, whether listening to music together or grinding in competitive matches for diamond rank. &lt;strong&gt;Join us in our mission! Your future is just a click away!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discord is committed to inclusion and providing reasonable accommodations during the interview process. &lt;/strong&gt;We want you to feel set up for success, so if you are in need of reasonable accommodations, please let your recruiter know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please see our Applicant and Candidate Privacy Policy for details regarding Discord’s collection and usage of personal information relating to the application and recruitment process by clicking&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://discord.com/terms/applicant-candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;HERE.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for a Senior Director of Publishing Production to join an unannounced game team remotely in the United States.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play, every day - whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues, or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing and innovating the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people around the world daily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are in the development stages of one of our new unannounced projects, and are looking for passionate game makers to collaborate, get in early and make their mark on this exciting venture!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Director of Production, you will lead &lt;strong&gt;Publishing Production&lt;/strong&gt; for one of Scopely&#39;s newest mobile titles. Reporting to the VP of Production, you&#39;ll sit at the intersection of Publishing, Development, and Marketing, ensuring ambitious ideas become exceptional player experiences through operational excellence, clear execution and trusted cross-functional partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for a production leader who enjoys turning strategy into action, thrives in complex cross-functional environments, and isn&#39;t afraid to roll up their sleeves to solve difficult execution challenges while continuously improving how teams work together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Publishing Production for the project, translating strategic priorities into coordinated execution across Development, Marketing, Licensing, Live Operations and Publishing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary operational bridge between Development and Publishing, ensuring product roadmaps, marketing campaigns, licensing initiatives and player-facing moments remain aligned from planning through execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive end-to-end execution of major publishing initiatives, including soft launch, global launch, integrated marketing campaigns, licensed IP activations, community moments and other high-impact player experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate strategic direction into actionable execution by establishing clear ownership, priorities, planning frameworks and decision-making rhythms that enable teams to move quickly and confidently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted partnerships across Product, Development, Marketing, Community, User Acquisition, CRM, Customer Experience and external partners, aligning diverse teams around shared objectives while navigating competing priorities and dependencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance immediate execution with long-term operational excellence by stepping directly into complex production challenges, removing blockers and continuously improving the systems, processes and ways of working behind them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Live Operations, Release Management and Development teams to ensure publishing priorities are fully integrated into release schedules and operational readiness, while maintaining clear ownership across organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide meaningful production visibility to senior leadership through clear communication, risk management, health reporting and actionable recommendations that support informed decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a growing Publishing Production function, establishing high standards for execution, collaboration and accountability while creating an environment where producers can operate with increasing autonomy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading Production, Publishing Production or Program Management within a mobile live-service game, partnering closely with both Development and Publishing organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience delivering complex cross-functional publishing initiatives, including product launches, integrated marketing campaigns, licensing or external partnerships, and large-scale player-facing experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of mobile game development and publishing, including the operational complexity, release cadence and planning required to support successful live-service games&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to translate strategic priorities into clear execution plans while remaining hands-on enough to remove blockers, resolve ambiguity and keep teams moving forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience influencing peers and senior leaders to drive alignment across multiple organizations without relying on direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to establish scalable production practices, governance and planning processes that improve execution quality, predictability and organizational effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading and developing producers or production leaders while fostering ownership, accountability and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment balancing player experience, development realities, publishing priorities, operational risk and business objectives in a fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, with the ability to tailor messaging and build alignment across technical, creative and business audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping or operating successful mobile free-to-play games&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with licensed IPs and complex external partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting games through soft launch, global launch and long-term live operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with co-development studios or globally distributed development teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering closely with Marketing, User Acquisition, CRM, Community or Customer Experience organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with release management, incident management or operational readiness for large-scale live games&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For candidates in CA, CO, NJ, NY, and WA, the annual salary range is provided below. In addition to base pay, employees may be eligible for equity, bonuses, and a comprehensive benefits package, including healthcare benefits, retirement benefits, pet insurance, paid holidays, paid Scopely free days, and unlimited paid time off. Base pay offered may vary depending on job-related knowledge, skills, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;CA, CO, NJ, NY, and WA Annual Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$193,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$284,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
